# Social cards

A link to a page shared anywhere renders as a grey rectangle without one,
which for a project whose pitch is that things should look considered is the
most visible unconsidered surface it has.

The default design system draws one per page, from its own tokens:

![A card: the site name in small capitals above a bold page title, with an
accent rule down the left edge](~/example-card.png)

That image is a *copy*, committed to `static/`, not the card this page
generates. Embedding the real one would tie this page to a design system that
draws cards — and the [link checker](../routing/) says so, which is how the
first draft of this page was caught.

Nothing is configured. A site with a `url` gets cards; a site without one does
not, because a card is only ever fetched from an absolute URL and drawing one
nothing will request is work for nobody.

## It is a separate crate, on purpose

`crabbucket-og` costs **76 transitive crates** and a few seconds of
compilation — a rasteriser, a text shaper and a font database. A docs site
with no interest in social previews should pay neither, so `crabbucket` does
not depend on it. A design system that wants cards does:

```rust
fn og_image(&self, page: &Page<'_, Layout>) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {
    let card = crabbucket_og::Card {
        title: &page.meta.title,
        site: &page.config.title,
        palette: crabbucket_og::Palette {
            background: hex(tok::color::SURFACE),
            foreground: hex(tok::color::TEXT),
            muted: hex(tok::color::TEXT_MUTED),
            accent: hex(tok::color::ACCENT),
        },
    };

    crabbucket_og::cached(&page.cache.join("og"), &card).ok()
}
```

The colours come from the same token file as the site itself, so a card looks
like the thing it links to without anybody restating the palette.

:::callout{kind = "note", title = "Why `hex()`"}
A token is a `var(--color-text, #e7eaf0)` reference, so a runtime theme
override reaches it. An image is drawn before any browser exists, so it needs
the value the reference falls back to.
:::

## The cache is not optional

A card costs about 65ms. Thirteen pages is most of a second, on a build that
otherwise takes a tenth of one:

```
cold   0.37s
warm   0.12s
```

So cards are cached in `.crabbucket/`, beside the site rather than inside
`dist/`, which is deleted every build. The key covers everything that changes
the picture — the words, the colours, the size, and a layout version bumped by
hand — so a hit is only ever the same image. Deleting the directory costs time
and nothing else.

## The font is bundled

Public Sans, under the SIL Open Font License, as two static instances.

Bundled rather than found on the machine, because an image generated during a
build has to look the same everywhere the build runs, and a font the build
merely hopes to find does not give that.

